# Machine-generated by scripts/security_scan.py — a hash of current content,
# not something to version. Committing a stale marker would just recreate
# the "scan once, edit quietly" gap the marker exists to close.
.security-scan-passed

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Packaged skill artifacts (scripts/security_scan.py --package output)
*.skill

# Pinned third-party clones — comparison-arm codebases and audit-pilot source
# corpora alike (their own git history, not our code, often 100M+ — the
# pinned commit/tag is recorded in benchmark/vendored/README.md instead,
# which stays tracked) — and the harness's scratch run output (regenerated
# by run_authoring.py, same convention as any other eval-engine workspace
# in this project). Was an explicit per-repo list; every repo vendored since
# audit-pilot Phase 8 (50+ dirs) was missing from it and showing up untracked
# in every `git status` since. Blanket pattern instead, self-maintaining.
/benchmark/vendored/*/
!/benchmark/vendored/README.md
/benchmark/harness/workspace/

# Session-scratch continuity note for resuming after a /clear — not project
# documentation, shouldn't be versioned.
/benchmark/SESSION_HANDOFF.md
